 """
-VLA inference runner — NO ROS 2 DEPENDENCY.
+VLA inference runner — action output over ZMQ or ROS 2.
 
 Runs an Isaac-GR00T VLA policy against the Sonic whole-body control stack.
-All communication uses ZMQ:
-  1. Robot state  -> ZMQ SUB on ``g1_debug`` topic (from C++ zmq_output_handler)
-  2. Actions out  -> ZMQ PUB (latent protocol v4: motion token + hand joints)
-  3. Camera       -> ZMQ/TCP via ComposedCameraClientSensor
-  4. Keyboard     -> ZMQ SUB via ZMQKeyboardSubscriber
+
+Transport choice controls only the action-output path (``--transport``):
+
+  transport=zmq (default)
+    1. Robot state  -> ZMQ SUB on ``g1_debug`` topic (from C++ zmq_output_handler)
+    2. Actions out  -> ZMQ PUB (Protocol v4: motion token + hand joints)
+                       AND ZMQ 'command' topic (start/stop/mode switch)
+    3. Camera       -> ZMQ/TCP via ComposedCameraClientSensor
+    4. Keyboard     -> ZMQ SUB via ZMQKeyboardSubscriber
+
+  transport=ros2
+    1-3 as above, but Actions out -> ROS 2 publisher on
+    ``ControlPolicy/vla_token`` (std_msgs/ByteMultiArray). The payload is the
+    same Protocol-v4 packed header+body, with an added ``toggle_vla_mode``
+    field that edge-triggers ENTER/EXIT VLA on the C++ side
+    (see ros2_input_handler.hpp::parse_packed_vla_token). 
 
 Uses the Isaac-GR00T PolicyClient (ZMQ REQ/REP) to communicate with a
 running PolicyServer.
 
 Keyboard commands (received via ZMQ from the standalone keyboard publisher):
-  p  -> pause / resume the policy loop
-  k  -> start / stop the C++ control loop
-  i  -> send initial pose and switch to POSE mode
+  p  -> pause / resume the policy loop (local only; never a mode toggle)
+  k  -> ZMQ:  start / stop the C++ control loop
+        ROS2: Toggle, mirroring ZMQ. First press sends toggle_policy_action=True
+              on ControlPolicy/upper_body_pose so the deploy STARTs the planner
+              without entering VLA (use 'i' to then enter VLA). Second press
+              sends another pulse to STOP: the deploy EXITs VLA via safety
+              reset.
+  i  -> send initial pose. In ROS 2 mode, the first ``i`` after startup
+        also sets ``toggle_vla_mode=True`` to enter VLA mode.
   t  -> change prompt at runtime (publisher sends ``prompt:<text>``)
   [  -> toggle left hand open/closed for initial pose
   ]  -> toggle right hand open/closed for initial pose
   c  -> start recording (handled by data exporter if running)
   s  -> stop recording success (handled by data exporter)
   f  -> stop recording failure (handled by data exporter)
+
+On Ctrl+C: same as ZMQ mode — just close the publisher. The ROS 2 deploy's
+token-freshness watchdog (TOKEN_FRESHNESS_MS_ in ros2_input_handler.hpp)
+falls back to encoder+planner automatically once tokens stop arriving; no
+explicit exit-VLA toggle is sent.
 """
 
